        "title": "Report: iPad shipments drop 27.5% as global tablet market plunges in Q3",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/05/report-ipad-shipments-drop-27-5-as-global-tablet-market-plunges-in-q3/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/ipad-pro-ipados-26-5-lock-screen.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Despite global iPad shipments dropping 27.5% year-over-year in the third calendar quarter, Apple maintained its lead in the tablet market, according to a new report released today. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl,ipad,omdia\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077693\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/05/report-ipad-shipments-drop-27-5-as-global-tablet-market-plunges-in-q3/#more-1077693\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
