        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/09/apple-staff-accused-of-signing-up-customers-to-subscriptions-without-consent-company-responds/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/11/Apple-staff-accused-of-signing-up-customers-to-subscriptions-without-consent.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1500\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Repair technician turned consumer rights advocate Louis Rossmann recently accused <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/apple-store/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Apple store</a> staff of signing up customers to the company’s services subscriptions without their consent.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has not yet commented, but has taken two steps indicating that the company takes the accusations seriously …</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"aapl,apple-stores\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077954\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/09/apple-staff-accused-of-signing-up-customers-to-subscriptions-without-consent-company-responds/#more-1077954\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
