        "title": "Raycast combines voice dictation and screen awareness in new AI feature",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/06/raycast-combines-voice-dictation-and-screen-awareness-in-new-ai-feature/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/11/raycast-dictate-ai.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Following the recent release of Screen Awareness, Raycast got an interesting update this week that lets users talk to AI about whatever is on their screen without having to explain the context. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apps,raycast\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077801\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/06/raycast-combines-voice-dictation-and-screen-awareness-in-new-ai-feature/#more-1077801\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
